# SD: Dedicated Task Plan definition

Status: draft
Gate: SD
Gate approval: open
Based on: PRD
Date: 2026-10-15
Owner: AGDF maintainer
Traceability contract: criteria-chain-v1
Design Decisions contract: sd-decisions-v1

## 1. Solution Overview

Add tp-definition as a focused semantic author using the existing definition-skill pattern. The implementation extends canonical plugin registration, a pure Core assignment phase, existing source inspection, explicit draft-revision transport and derived host assets. It reuses the current TP template and typed recording/presentation transactions.

Flow: current request activation -> canonical target/run assignment -> existing gate evaluation and approved-source checks -> tp_definition continuation -> draft/clarify only the bound unapproved TP -> existing artefact recording -> fresh gate-check -> existing exact presentation and deliberate Approval: TP. Approved TP still leads through pre-implementation Brownfield Analysis before implementation. No new gate, executor, writer or state store is introduced.

The approved PRD fixes the product scope. The completed Brownfield Review identifies preparation, correction, source-inspection and generation owners. This design resolves its remaining architectural questions; test-command enumeration and execution scheduling belong in the subsequent TP.

## 2. Ownership And Source Of Truth

| Concern | Authoritative owner | Design effect |
