| Product acceptance | Approved run-local PRD.md | Reference existing criterion IDs; never recreate acceptance prose as another product register. |
| Skill identity, discovery and contract inventory | plugins/agdf/meta/agdf-plugin.definition.json | Register tp-definition once with judgement_required dispatch and tp-definition/gate-artifact-preparation runtime modules. |
| Semantic TP authoring | New plugins/agdf/skills/tp-definition/SKILL.md and meta/contracts/tp-definition.md | Bound drafting, clarification and explicit permitted revision only; remove competing semantic ownership from gate-check/shared guidance. |
| Assignment and safe source facts | packages/core/lib/skill-dispatch/ and control-evaluation/definition-sources.js | Add tpDefinitionPhase; reuse canonical evaluation and contained-source inspection. |
| Readiness and correction routing | control-evaluation/gate-check.js, traceability-readiness.js and control-state/presentation-decision.js | TP preparation and remediation select tp-definition; existing gate evaluation remains authoritative. |
| Template and recording | Existing plugin TP.md template, resources/artefact-templates.js and control-state/run-artefact-recording.js | Extend the same template; retain typed source binding, history, locks and transaction recovery. |
| Approval and source revision | Existing run-presentation and approval/source-revision services | Preserve exact material, deliberate new replies and protected approved sources. |
| Host/package propagation | scripts/sync-request-activation-projections.js, scripts/sync-package-assets.js and existing package build | Generate current host profiles and runtime from canonical sources; no manual derived-owner edits. |
| Post-implementation fulfilment | task-plan-review and qa-gate under quality.md | Review obligations and actual evidence, with qa-gate retaining the sole technical QA decision. |

## 3. Architecture Decisions

- SDD-001: Register one focused tp-definition skill and contract; rationale: match the established definition roles while giving TP content one semantic owner; consequence: registry, router/help and generated references must agree, while gate-check retains control and task-plan-review retains fulfilment review.
- SDD-002: Add a pure tpDefinitionPhase over current evaluated state and typed source facts; rationale: assignment must not duplicate gate permission, source integrity or persistence; consequence: missing prerequisites and unrelated blockers remain outside authoring, and source inspection must locate Brownfield Review by type rather than position.
- SDD-003: Add tp_action revise and CLI --tp-action revise through the existing revision-bound gate-check resume-intake transport; rationale: ready drafts need explicit editing intent rather than selection-based authority; consequence: ordinary/direct ready-draft continuation presents current content, and unsupported revision requests fail explicitly rather than becoming successful status reads.
- SDD-004: Reuse the existing TP-derived_from-SD typed recording and exact presentation/approval services; rationale: one persistence and approval authority already protects sources and history; consequence: no new writer, receipt schema, source-revision service or control-data migration, and changed drafts always require a new presentation and reply.
- SDD-005: Extend the existing TP template and TP readiness owner with declared planning decisions and evidence-obligation details for new plans; rationale: ID coverage alone cannot establish executable planning or block unresolved material execution choices; consequence: a versioned plan-local declaration enables deterministic completeness checks while semantic usefulness remains a review obligation and unmarked historical plans retain existing behavior.
- SDD-006: Project skill names, request guards, contracts and dispatcher arguments through existing host/package generators; rationale: supported consumers need one canonical interface; consequence: all derived surfaces and payload/footprint guards must be checked, with no live install or budget increase implied.
- SDD-007: Verify the actual production assignment, recording and decision paths plus a concrete semantic planning exercise; rationale: copied instruction/schema tests cannot demonstrate the requested behavior; consequence: combine focused deterministic negative cases and package checks with retained authored-plan evidence, and distinguish those from unobserved loaded/native-host qualification.

## 4. Integration Points

### Bound assignment and sources

Add packages/core/lib/skill-dispatch/tp-definition.js, adjacent to prd-definition.js and sd-definition.js. Its pure phase returns null unless the requested run matches the evaluated state, the current gate is TP, mode is structured_slice or structured_delivery, Brownfield Review is complete/not_applicable, PRD and SD artefacts and approvals are approved, TP is unapproved, source reassessment is not pending and the current revision is available. Reject conflicting UR/PRD/SD authoring actions, foreign TP destination paths and any doctor integrity findings. Eligible blocking reasons are none and the existing AGDF_TP_TRACEABILITY_INCOMPLETE for specifically diagnosed incomplete unapproved TP content; no other blocker is relaxed.

Invoke only for actual direct tp-definition work or authorized gate-check intake/continue_delivery. A read-only gate-check request does not assign authoring. For a registered ready TP, require explicit revision-bound tp_action revise before returning the phase, including direct-skill calls; otherwise use existing gate-check presentation. An incomplete registered TP can receive a condition-specific correction continuation without turning status into delivery. Discovery/loading remains non-authorizing even when a continuation exists.

Integrate phase assignment before generic judgement handling in skill-dispatch/service.js. Add tp-definition to the existing unbound definition inventory, ignoreRunIdEnv and safe gate-check fallback paths. A direct invocation at another gate must never fall through to a generic judgement writer. Align TP requiredGateArtifactPreparation and presentation-decision remediation with the same owner. If an explicit tp_action cannot produce the eligible phase, return the existing draft_revision_route_unavailable diagnostic and appropriate existing source-revision recovery for approved material.

Use inspectDefinitionSources with explicit PRD, SD and Brownfield Review source types. Replace its positional sources[1] Brownfield assumption with typed lookup, preserving existing PRD/SD behavior. The same helper keeps containment, symlink, digest and required UX-input checks; existing Core evaluation continues to own approval, seal and analytical applicability. No duplicated source validator or TP-specific UX policy. Return exact source paths/digests, canonical target/run/revision/destination, plugin template, registered-draft flag and resolved artefact/presentation languages in phase tp_definition with skill_id tp-definition and authorizes false.

### Revision and preservation

Extend the shared dispatch contract, argument normalization, function schema, documented binding arguments and CLI parsing/validation/forwarding with tp_action/tpAction/--tp-action. Permit only revise on gate-check with intake true, intake_mode resume, run_id and expected_revision_id; exclude all other authoring actions and continue_delivery. Keep schema/CLI parity and canonical registered host aliases. The existing writer rechecks current stage, revision and protected material; this transport itself grants no authority.

The author uses the supplied installed TP template and current approved sources. Initial recording remains update_draft false. An explicitly permitted replacement uses true with fresh reviewed mapping/input files; the writer preserves prior proof and other bound bytes. Relationship remains TP derived_from SD. PRD is retained as an exact approved planning source without introducing another relationship registry. After recording, redispatch gate-check and prepare its exact presentation; previous presentations and replies cannot approve changed content. Approved-source changes use the existing separately reviewed source-revision route.

### Plan content and material decisions

Retain Task List, Verification Traceability, Test Plan, Brownfield Scope, Out Of Scope, Risks And Blockers and Next Step in the canonical TP template. Add guidance and an Evidence Obligations table within Test Plan with columns: criterion_id, scenario_id, test_route, environment, prerequisites_permissions, owner, expected_evidence, unavailable_action. Each applicable verification scenario has a row; shared routes may repeat references with concrete reasons. Explicit not_applicable needs a reason. The skill checks content semantically and asks one focused bundled question when material planning information is missing. An unavailable prerequisite may have a resolved plan for an explicit evidence gap; it is never a claimed pass or access authorization.

New tp-definition drafts declare Planning Decisions contract: tp-decisions-v1 and exactly one Planning Decisions table: Decision, Source, Status, Resolution, Owner. Source is TP for a local planning decision, or SD: followed by the exact decision label from the approved SD Design Decisions table with timing later_tp. Include each such SD row exactly once, including its already-resolved execution context; local names must be unique. Status is resolved or open. All rows need concrete resolution/context and named owners; an open row blocks TP readiness. With no material choice, record one resolved applicability row with Source TP. Product or architecture choices cannot be resolved by this table and route upstream.

Extend evaluateTpTraceability as the sole TP readiness aggregation owner to include the declared planning-decision completeness check. Keep any pure parsing helper subordinate to that owner. Reuse the existing SD decision parser's normalized read-only rows by extracting/exporting its current parsing facts without changing SD readiness policy. Do not introduce a second SD table grammar. Validate the supported unique TP declaration/table, row fields, unique names and exact SD later_tp coverage. Feed open items through existing AGDF_TP_TRACEABILITY_INCOMPLETE, so gate-check, artifact-readiness, recording, run-present and approval observe the same failure. Extend the existing authoring-format descriptor and artefact-readiness projection as needed through those owners; no new gate or parallel readiness service.

Unmarked historical TP documents retain existing traceability behavior. New/explicitly rewritten tp-definition drafts must retain their declaration and table; removing them to evade checks is prohibited and tested against the authoring contract. Already approved bytes and receipts are never rewritten. Structural checks observe declared completeness, not undiscovered semantic truth; task-plan-review and QA still assess the real plan and evidence.

### Canonical propagation

Update canonical plugin skill/module registration, runtime-contract manifest references, router/help and affected role descriptions together. Project activation guards, host aliases and runtime bindings through the existing generators. Adjust CLI/MCP dispatch forwarding and tests through their current shared contract; do not edit active installed plugins or another run. Existing package checks validate generated Codex/Claude, prefixed Copilot and OpenCode surfaces. If a payload/footprint guard fails, first reduce duplication within the approved canonical design; unresolved limits require visible scope reconsideration, not a silent baseline increase.

## 5. Constraints And Compatibility

No new gate, permission, persistent schema, writer, transaction or approval formula. The optional declared TP planning format extends new draft content; it does not migrate existing approved plans or retroactively reinterpret legacy proof. Current Core gate/source validation stays authoritative. New runtime/template/skill assets must ship coherently in the same generated package; mixed versions fail existing version/provenance checks rather than falling back to repository templates.

Avoid broad abstraction of all definition phases during this change. Reuse narrow helpers where semantic assumptions match; retain stage-specific eligibility. Existing UR/PRD/SD dispatch, source inspection and explicit revision behavior need regression checks after typed source lookup and argument extensions. No host install, external access, release or publication is authorized by this SD. Existing macOS/local checks do not establish Windows or loaded-host support.

## 6. Test And Evidence Strategy

Use production Core/CLI/MCP entry points against isolated controlled run fixtures with approved PRD/SD. Cover initial eligible assignment; direct/unbound request with misleading ambient run; stage/revision/foreign-path/approved-source/integrity rejection; read-only status; ready-draft presentation without editing; valid explicit revision; incomplete traceability and declared planning-decision correction; upstream reassessment and missing/unsafe installed-template/source behavior. Preserve existing PRD/SD behavior under typed source lookup and mutually exclusive action parsing.

Readiness checks must reject malformed/duplicate/unknown planning declarations, open decisions, missing owners/resolutions, duplicated/unknown SD references and missing later_tp coverage. A complete resolved plan passes; legacy unmarked plans retain current behavior. Verify evidence-obligation guidance and a concrete missing-access planning example semantically; table existence alone is not proof. Cross-check correction ownership and unchanged task-plan-review/qa-gate authority.

Exercise actual typed initial recording and permitted replacement, exact source bindings/history, preserved protected bytes, fresh presentation and old-response rejection. Production MCP/CLI schemas and negative flags must agree. Run the affected dispatch/traceability/SD, request-activation, skill-conformance/eval, generation, package-content and footprint/payload checks appropriate to the final diff; expand only for unresolved failures or changed shared owners.

Retain a bounded production-continuation authoring exercise using the prepared exact-version package against an isolated target, with returned continuation, actual authored plan, deferred SD-decision dispositions, evidence-obligation rows and semantic review. This is cooperative agent evidence; no independent proof or general model reliability claim. TP specifies commands, fixture construction, environments, access/owners and report paths. Native loaded-host lanes not actually observed remain explicit gaps; no global installation or foreign configuration changes are prerequisites to the deterministic checks.

